{% set local_problem %}
<p>Many New Market homes have been standing for generations — and that's a lot of years for water to damage fascia boards. When gutters leak or overflow, water soaks into wood and causes rot that spreads if not addressed.</p>

<p>Older homes often have original fascia that's been repainted over damage rather than properly repaired. That hidden rot affects gutter attachment and can spread to structural elements.</p>

<p>We see this regularly on New Market properties: homes that need gutters, but first need the fascia repaired so those gutters have something solid to attach to.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>We start with careful inspection, checking fascia and soffit for water damage, soft spots, and rot. We'll show you what we find.</p>

<p>For damaged sections, we remove existing gutters, cut out bad wood, and install new fascia using quality materials appropriate for your home.</p>

<p>Then we install new gutters on the solid foundation — properly attached and designed to prevent future damage.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've been repairing fascia on New Market homes for over 20 years. We understand older construction and know how to match materials for seamless repairs.</p>

<p>Our crews handle both carpentry and gutters. One company, one warranty, one point of contact.</p>
{% endset %}
